From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Shenk <kevin@avu.nu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:18:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Honour the connection's optional capabilities

A remote connection may withhold transactions, savepoints, temporary tables
and user-defined functions. Transactional statements then go through the
"transaction_fallback" option ("warn", "error" or "ignore"), with the PDO
API's begin/commit/rollback contract still upheld by an emulated flag;
CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE is refused and the temporary information schema
skipped; the user-defined functions are registered only where they can
run, and the flag that says so is what the next patch's translator keys on.
---
 .../src/sqlite/class-wp-mysql-on-sqlite.php   | 161 +++++++++++++++++-
 ...s-wp-sqlite-information-schema-builder.php |   9 +
 2 files changed, 164 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

